Here's a template for calculating the offset of an element in an array:

```c
// Define the array and the index of the element you want to find the offset of
int array[10];
int index = 5;

// Calculate the offset of the element at the specified index
int offset = array[index] - array[0];

// Print the offset
printf("%d\n", offset);
```

This template assumes that the array is 0-indexed, meaning the first element is at index 0. If your array is 1-indexed, you would need to adjust the offset calculation accordingly.

